  "guideS1Title": "1. Enter the city",
  "guideS1L1": "The first time you open the app, confirm you are 18 or older and allow precise location while using the app. Without precise location the radar can't work.",
  "guideS1L2": "Write one sentence about how you feel right now (up to 20 characters), agree to the Terms of Use and Privacy Policy, and tap Check in here and enter.",
  "guideS1L3": "No phone number, email or real name is needed. Your account is anonymous and tied to this phone.",
  "guideS1L4": "Words in your mood set its colour: “happy, laugh” is gold, “sad, cry” is blue, “angry” is orange-red, “calm, daydream” is green, “fired up” is orange, “love, heart” is pink, and anything else is soft violet.",
  "guideS1L5": "Checking in: every time you open the app you check in yourself, and only then can people nearby see your mood and roughly where you are, and you see them. It never happens automatically. Others see the place where you checked in; it doesn't follow you around. If you move more than 1 km away, Check in here appears below the radar. If the app has been in the background for more than 30 minutes, you check in again when you come back.",
  "guideS2Title": "2. The bottom bar",
  "guideS2L1": "Tap your own photo on the left to edit your photo, city name (up to 10 characters) and mood.",
  "guideS2L2": "Notepad icon: leave a whisper right here.",
  "guideS2L3": "Share icon: turn your mood into a night-scene card.",
  "guideS2L4": "Sliders icon on the far right: open Settings.",
  "guideS3Title": "3. Radar and bubbles",
  "guideS3L1": "Mood bubbles from people within 5 km appear on the radar. Only a rough distance band is shown (such as “within 100 m”), never an address.",
  "guideS3L2": "A breathing bubble means the person is using the app. A dimmed bubble marked Resting means their screen is locked, and you can still knock. A grey bubble with no name is a fading echo left by someone who just left, and it slowly fades away.",
  "guideS3L3": "Pinch to zoom the map. Turn your phone and the radar turns with you.",
  "guideS3L4": "When bubbles crowd together they merge into a glowing orb, “N moods here”. Tap it to fan them out in a ring so each one can be tapped; tap the middle or empty space to close it.",
  "guideS3L5": "Names starting with Demo belong to demo people who reply automatically. They aren't real, and you can use them to try every feature.",
  "guideS3L6": "When no one is nearby, “You are tonight's first light” appears at the bottom, and you can invite friends to light up your block.",
  "guideS4Title": "4. Knocking and chatting",
  "guideS4L1": "Long-press someone's bubble → Knock. They have 5 minutes to accept, decline or skip. While you wait, a line of light flows from you to them.",
  "guideS4L2": "Once they accept, a chat starts with a 10-minute countdown. Any new message restarts it, and the chat ends when you both go quiet.",
  "guideS4L3": "When the chat ends, the messages are deleted from the server. The other person could still take screenshots, so share with care.",
  "guideS4L4": "When someone knocks on your door, a knock card appears. You can accept, decline, skip or report right away.",
  "guideS5Title": "5. Glimmers",
  "guideS5L1": "Double-tap someone's bubble, or long-press and choose Send a glimmer, to let them know someone noticed without saying a word.",
  "guideS5L2": "They only see “N glimmers resonated with you tonight” and never who sent them. You can send the same person one glimmer every 24 hours.",
  "guideS6Title": "6. Whispers",
  "guideS6L1": "Tap the notepad icon in the bottom bar to leave a sentence where you are (up to 60 characters).",
  "guideS6L2": "For the next 7 days, anyone within 300 m will see an envelope on the radar and can open it to read.",
  "guideS6L3": "Whispers are always anonymous. You can have up to 3 at a time, leave at most 1 every 10 minutes, and take them back at any time.",
  "guideS6L4": "Letters to the future: when writing a whisper, choose To my future self, then one month or one year. Only you can see it. When the time comes you'll be notified, and it opens on its own when you're back within 100 m. It can be read only once. Only you see a small hourglass on the radar (locked or unlocked), and it can't be tapped. You can have up to 5 at a time; see or delete them in Settings → My letters to the future.",
  "guideS7Title": "7. City mood weather",
  "guideS7L1": "The label at the top left shows the most common mood within 20 km over the last 24 hours. Tap it for the full breakdown.",
  "guideS7L2": "Shares are hidden when fewer than 10 people took part, so no one can be identified.",
  "guideS8Title": "8. Gatherings",
  "guideS8L1": "To start one: Settings → Host a gathering → enter a name, one emoji as its icon, and a start and end time (up to 24 hours) → Start gathering.",
  "guideS8L2": "The gathering covers 5 km around the place where the host checked in; when the host checks in again, it moves with them. The host has a ring of light and a Host label on the radar.",
  "guideS8L3": "The host can post announcements (as many as needed), ask everyone a question, and end the gathering at any time.",
  "guideS8L4": "To join, add the gathering's icon to your city name (for example “Wandering Cat🌈”). While you're in range you'll see the pinned announcement above the radar and get notifications. Remove the icon to leave.",
  "guideS8L5": "Group question: answer with a mood. The host only sees the overall mood shares, never who answered what, and shares are hidden below 10 answers.",
  "guideS8L6": "Only one gathering can use an icon in the same area at a time. Once it ends, anyone can use that icon.",
  "guideS8L7": "Hand-over: the host long-presses a participant's bubble → Hand over hosting, and chooses an announced or quiet hand-over. If the person accepts within 5 minutes they become host, and announcements and the question stay. The previous host becomes a participant and the icon is added to their name.",
  "guideS9Title": "9. City Beacon (accessible restrooms)",
  "guideS9L1": "Tap the restroom icon at the bottom left of the map to turn on the beacon. Gender-friendly, accessible and family restrooms within 2 km appear on the radar, with a count next to the icon. Tap the three round filters above it to show only some kinds.",
  "guideS9L2": "Tap a marker to see the floor, facilities and distance, and tap Walk there to get directions in your map app.",
  "guideS9L3": "Data comes from Taiwan's Ministry of Environment public restroom records and is updated monthly. Opening hours aren't included; “Probably open at night” is our estimate based on the type of place.",
  "guideS9L4": "If something is wrong you can report it (not gender-friendly, closed at night, can't find it). When 3 people report the same problem, the marker turns grey with a note.",
  "guideS10Title": "10. Mood cards and mood trail",
  "guideS10L1": "The share button in the bottom bar turns your current mood into a night-scene card, made for Instagram Stories. The card never shows your location.",
  "guideS10L2": "Settings → My mood trail lets you look back at the moods and places you've written. It's stored only on your phone, and you can turn it off or clear it at any time.",
  "guideS11Title": "13. Settings and notifications",
  "guideS11L1": "Nightly reminder: a gentle reminder at 21:30 every night. Turn it on or off in Settings.",
  "guideS11L2": "Knocks, new messages, glimmers and gathering announcements arrive as notifications. You can turn them off in your phone's settings.",
  "guideS11L3": "Every Friday from 21:00 to 23:00 is Light-up Night, when everyone comes online together and the city shines brightest.",
  "guideS12Title": "14. Reporting and blocking",
  "guideS12L1": "You can report from a bubble's long-press menu, a knock card, the top right of a chat, a whisper or a gathering announcement. Once you report, that person or post disappears from your screen right away and the chat ends. We handle every report within 24 hours.",
  "guideS12L2": "Moods, names, whispers, chat messages and gathering announcements are automatically filtered for offensive words and contact details such as phone numbers and links.",
  "guideS12L3": "Once you block someone, you disappear from each other's radar and can't knock or send glimmers. Unblock them in Settings → Blocked people.",
  "guideS12L4": "If you're in immediate danger, call your local emergency number (110 in Taiwan).",
  "guideS13Title": "15. Privacy and your account",
  "guideS13L1": "Only after you check in can people nearby see your mood, city name, photo and rough distance. They see the place where you checked in, not your live location.",
  "guideS13L2": "Settings → Delete account and data permanently erases everything you left in the city, at any time.",
  "guideS13L3": "Questions? Go to Settings → Contact us, or email service.softchip@gmail.com.",
  "guideS14Title": "11. Parallel Universe",
  "guideS14L1": "Tap the globe at the top right of the radar to turn it on, and again to turn it off. It's off every time you open the app.",
  "guideS14L2": "Each city or county in Taiwan is centred on its own central station (Greater Taipei on Taipei Station, Taoyuan on Taoyuan Station, and so on) and matched with cities abroad: Japan, Korea, Hong Kong, Macau, Singapore, Malaysia, Indonesia and Vietnam. Cities abroad are matched with Taiwan.",
  "guideS14L3": "However far and in whichever direction you are from your station, that's where you appear in theirs, the same distance and direction from their station, blurred to about 500 m. No one can see your real location.",
  "guideS14L4": "You see each other if either of you has it on: with it on, you see everyone in the matched cities who has the app open; with it off, you only see people who turned it on. Only people who have checked in and have the app open appear in other cities.",
  "guideS14L5": "People from Parallel Universe have a dashed ring and show their city. You can still send glimmers, knock and chat. Fading echoes, whispers, letters to the future and gatherings stay local.",
  "guideS15Title": "12. Translation",
  "guideS15L1": "In a chat, when a message isn't in your language, Tap to translate appears under it. Tap to translate it into your language, and tap again to see the original.",
  "guideS15L2": "Mood bubbles on the radar work the same way: when one isn't in your language, tap it to translate and tap again to go back to the original.",
  "guideS15L3": "Translation happens entirely on your phone; the text is never uploaded. iPhone uses Apple's built-in translation, and the system asks before downloading a language the first time. Android uses Google ML Kit, which asks you first and then downloads a language model of about 30 MB. iPhone can't translate Malay yet.",
  "guideIntro": "Mood Whisper is a city at night: write one sentence about how you feel right now, and see how the people near you feel.",
